{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de4b8aa20fc16230f14b50", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Oscillations - Test 1", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295e48"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295ccb", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c64", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e8587"], "question": {"text": "A particle executes simple harmonic motion between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></math>. If time taken by particle to go from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>; then time taken by particle in going from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is:"}, "options": [{"id": "590ceb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c65"}, {"id": "769ebf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c66"}, {"id": "4c6810", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c67"}, {"id": "bc2ce8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c68"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c69", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b85"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d42"], "question": {"text": "<p>The variation of displacement with time of a particle executing free simple harmonic motion is shown in the figure.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F2b84d4f3-9e44-4d07-8f56-acd7c2558b73-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 437px; height: 149px;\" /></p><p>The potential energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> versus time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math> plot of the particle is correctly shown in figure:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "ad71d5", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F07c96215-1e0f-46d0-a430-fc4135e08d13-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 383px; height: 140px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c6a"}, {"id": "b7ba5c", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F713e3112-c7bf-412b-8fe4-b0ad2c9ea1d2-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 422px; height: 149px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c6b"}, {"id": "34cf33", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ff4fd0d4c-6e45-488e-bfa8-7a670c8df046-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 445px; height: 149px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c6c"}, {"id": "b5863f", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fa316fe59-7ddd-4d64-bc43-1b0ace65c697-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 461px; height: 151px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c6d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c6e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee5"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5df5"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements. One is labelled as Assertion (A) and the other is labelled as Reason (R).\nAssertion (A) : A simple pendulum is taken to a planet of mass and radius, 4 times and 2 times, respectively, than the Earth. The time period of the pendulum remains same on earth and the planet.\nReason (R): The mass of the pendulum remains unchanged at Earth and the other planet.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "d2f2f4", "text": "$(\\mathbf{A})$ is false but (R) is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c6f"}, {"id": "94ea49", "text": "(A) is true but (R) is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c70"}, {"id": "ee6585", "text": "Both $(\\mathbf{A})$ and $(\\mathbf{R})$ are true and $(\\mathbf{R})$ is the correct explanation of $(\\mathbf{A})$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c71"}, {"id": "ae2a34", "text": "Both (A) and (R) are true but (R) is NOT the correct explanation of (A)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c72"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c73", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b471a"], "question": {"text": "Two massless springs with spring constants <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math>, carry <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> masses at their free ends. These two masses oscillate vertically such that their maximum velocities are equal. Then, the ratio of their respective amplitudes will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "5114ec", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c74"}, {"id": "7b2ba5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c75"}, {"id": "755ac4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c76"}, {"id": "78a941", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c77"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c78", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b76e478ae845c43c6e2a"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d4d"], "question": {"text": "Two light identical springs of spring constant <math><mi>k</mi></math> are attached horizontally at the two ends of a uniform horizontal rod <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> of length <math><mi>l</mi></math> and mass <math><mi>m</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The rod is pivoted at its center &#39;<em>O</em>&#39; and can rotate freely in horizontal plane. The other ends of the two springs are fixed to rigid supports as shown in figure. The rod is gently pushed through a small angle and released. The frequency of resulting oscillation is:<br /><br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Frppapzkndfgzzenyrrbaihsaqisosoxpqjqwboerunkugghzqt.png?alt=media\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "66140f", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c79"}, {"id": "bd913c", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c7a"}, {"id": "a17708", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c7b"}, {"id": "e54a95", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c7c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c7d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b61"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b20"], "question": {"text": "The function of time representing a simple&nbsp;harmonic motion with a period of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>&#969;</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is :"}, "options": [{"id": "7d20cf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c7e"}, {"id": "4f4008", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c7f"}, {"id": "553848", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c80"}, {"id": "126d66", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c81"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c82", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b85"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b53"], "question": {"text": "<p>The displacement time graph of a particle executing SHM is given in figure: (sketch is schematic and not to scale)&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fc6f0a451-f035-4e15-aa77-5ea5042011b4-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 423px; height: 232px;\" /></p><p>Which of the following statements is/are true for this motion?&nbsp;</p><p>(A) The force is zero at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>T</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math><br />(B) The magnitude of acceleration is maximum at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></math><br />(C) The speed is maximum at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math><br />(D) The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>.</mo></math> is equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>.</mo></math> of the&nbsp;oscillation at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "2792ef", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c83"}, {"id": "617ec1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c84"}, {"id": "13176b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c85"}, {"id": "e36bed", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c86"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c87", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3e"], "question": {"text": "Two bodies A and B of equal mass are suspended from two massless springs of spring constant $k_1$ and $k_2$, respectively. If the bodies oscillate vertically such that their amplitudes are equal, the ratio of the maximum velocity of $A$ to the maximum velocity of $B$ is"}, "options": [{"id": "adc53a", "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{k}_1}{\\mathrm{k}_2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c88"}, {"id": "841304", "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{k}_1}{\\mathrm{k}_2}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c89"}, {"id": "8e6fa5", "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{k}_2}{\\mathrm{k}_1}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c8a"}, {"id": "fd1ff7", "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{k}_2}{\\mathrm{k}_1}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c8b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c8c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["6117b607478ae845c43c631c"], "question": {"text": "The motion of a simple pendulum executing S.H.M. is represented by the following equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, where time is measured in second. The length of pendulum is"}, "options": [{"id": "82bd4a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>97</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c8d"}, {"id": "b7dd77", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c8e"}, {"id": "492864", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>99</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c8f"}, {"id": "47a2d9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>406</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c90"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c91", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee5"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d33"], "question": {"text": "An object of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is suspended at the end of a massless wire of length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> and area of cross-section, A. Young modulus of the material of the wire is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math>. If the mass is pulled down slightly its frequency of oscillation along the vertical direction is :"}, "options": [{"id": "742449", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c92"}, {"id": "6dd3ea", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c93"}, {"id": "cfee91", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c94"}, {"id": "d7dff3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c95"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c96", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b76e478ae845c43c6e2a"], "concepts": ["612b2c79acaae91ef45d3832"], "question": {"text": "A rod of mass <math> <mi>M</mi> </math> and length <math> <mrow> <mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></mrow> </math> is suspended at its middle by a wire. It exhibits torsional oscillations. If two masses, each of mass&nbsp;<math><mi>m</mi></math>, are attached at a distance <math> <mrow> <mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow> </math> from its centre on both sides, it reduces the oscillation frequency by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math>. The value of ratio <math><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></math> is close to"}, "options": [{"id": "d71476", "text": "<math><mn>0.17</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c97"}, {"id": "b1eeca", "text": "<math><mn>0.77</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c98"}, {"id": "2c389e", "text": "<math><mn>0.57</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c99"}, {"id": "05e756", "text": "<math><mn>0.37</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c9a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c9b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["6162fb0e6ed13040ec84a8f7"], "question": {"text": "<p>For particle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;revolving round the centre <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> with radius of circular path <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> and regular velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi></math>, as shown in below figure, the projection of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi></math> on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F40424b7c-3f2d-42c6-80d3-c2a6dadfa149.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 201px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "9c5ace", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c9c"}, {"id": "a915e3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c9d"}, {"id": "8dd284", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c9e"}, {"id": "cddf71", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295c9f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295ca0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b85"], "concepts": ["6117b90767dbe2603c3e8f87"], "question": {"text": "A particle is executing simple harmonic motion <math><mo>(</mo><mi>S</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>)</mo></math> of amplitude <math><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo></math> along the <math><mi>x</mi></math> -axis, about <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math> When its potential Energy <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> equal kinetic energy <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> the position of the particle will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "450a19", "text": "<math><mi>A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295ca1"}, {"id": "221428", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295ca2"}, {"id": "8a556b", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295ca3"}, {"id": "7bc522", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295ca4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295ca5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee5"], "concepts": ["6176f4006581241c7072b9b2"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements. One is labelled as Assertion (A) and the other is labelled as Reason (R).\nAssertion (A) : Knowing initial position $x_0$ and initial momentum $p_0$ is enough to determine the position and momentum at any time $t$ for a simple harmonic motion with a given angular frequency $\\omega$.\nReason (R): The amplitude and phase can be expressed in terms of $x_0$ and $\\mathrm{p}_0$.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "3264b4", "text": "(A) is false but (R) is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295ca6"}, {"id": "848144", "text": "(A) is true but (R) is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295ca7"}, {"id": "2f9c34", "text": "Both (A) and (R) are true but (R) is NOT the correct explanation of (A)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295ca8"}, {"id": "e280da", "text": "Both $(\\mathbf{A})$ and $(\\mathbf{R})$ are true and $(\\mathbf{R})$ is the correct explanation of $(\\mathbf{A})$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295ca9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295caa", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["617aa9cbef3fe65ad8e81c30"], "question": {"text": "Two identical tennis balls each having mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;and charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;are suspended from a fixed point by threads of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>.</mo></math> What is the equilibrium separation when each thread makes a small angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> with the vertical?"}, "options": [{"id": "4e573e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cab"}, {"id": "0e7fc6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cac"}, {"id": "cc3d31", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cad"}, {"id": "8a7c0d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#960;&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cae"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295caf", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d2a"], "question": {"text": "When a particle executes simple Harmonic motion, the nature of graph of velocity as function of displacement will be"}, "options": [{"id": "b21844", "text": "Circular", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cb0"}, {"id": "ff9831", "text": "Ellipitical", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cb1"}, {"id": "db7fb9", "text": "Sinusoidal", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cb2"}, {"id": "56d786", "text": "Straight line", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cb3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cb4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdb66f9ce3f243b5641"], "question": {"text": "A light hollow cube of side length 10 cm and mass 10 g , is floating in water. It is pushed down and released to execute simple harmonic oscillations. The time period of oscillations is $y \\pi \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~s}$, where the value of $y$ is\n(Acceleration due to gravity, $g=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$, density of water $=10^3 \\mathrm{~kg} / \\mathrm{m}^3$ )"}, "options": [{"id": "688c57", "text": "$6$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cb5"}, {"id": "ba956b", "text": "$2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cb6"}, {"id": "cc5d15", "text": "$4$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cb7"}, {"id": "e91aba", "text": "$1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cb8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cb9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b85"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d42"], "question": {"text": "A particle executes SHM of amplitude<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi></math>. The distance from the mean position when its kinetic energy becomes equal to its potential energy is:"}, "options": [{"id": "c11894", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mi>A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cba"}, {"id": "41f401", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cbb"}, {"id": "063426", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cbc"}, {"id": "99c2ac", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cbd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cbe", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee5"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5df5"], "question": {"text": "&nbsp;A ring is hung on a nail. It can oscillate, without slipping or sliding (i) in its plane with a time period <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and (ii) back and forth in a direction perpendicular to its plane, with a period&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math>&nbsp;will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "1473b3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cbf"}, {"id": "2ae0ec", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cc0"}, {"id": "0ae418", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cc1"}, {"id": "8de1a3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cc2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cc3", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["60e567c3499d1e49588f9939"], "question": {"text": "Assume that a tunnel is dug along a chord of the earth, at a perpendicular distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> from the earth&#39;s centre, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is the radius of the earth. The wall of the tunnel is frictionless. If a particle is released in this tunnel, it will execute a simple harmonic motion with a time period:"}, "options": [{"id": "d7b469", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cc4"}, {"id": "e53d30", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mi>g</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cc5"}, {"id": "b3e1cc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cc6"}, {"id": "30ad4a", "text": "Image is virtual, opposite side of convex mirror.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cc7"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:30.188Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:30.188Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295e46"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295daa", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cf4", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e98"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3e"], "question": {"text": "The displacement of a particle executing SHM is given by $x=10 \\sin \\left(w t+\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) m$. The time period of motion is $3.14 \\mathrm{~s}$. The velocity of the particle at $t=0$ is ______$\\mathrm{m} / \\mathrm{s}$."}, "options": [{"id": "f806c8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cf5"}, {"id": "f7c715", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cf6"}, {"id": "8535b8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cf7"}, {"id": "67227d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cf8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cf9", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee5"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5df5"], "question": {"text": "A mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;attached to free end of a spring executes SHM with a period of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. If the mass is increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> the period of oscillation increases by one second, the value of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is ________ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kg</mi></math>.&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "b1b60a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cfa"}, {"id": "3116d0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cfb"}, {"id": "2c2162", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cfc"}, {"id": "facb99", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cfd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cfe", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b85"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d42"], "question": {"text": "The potential energy of a particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> in motion along the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>. The time period of the particle for small oscillation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#8771;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> is _____ ."}, "options": [{"id": "e05c80", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295cff"}, {"id": "195f7e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295d00"}, {"id": "371dc9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295d01"}, {"id": "a96faa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295d02"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295d03", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4764"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b471a"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the reported figure, two bodies <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;of masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> are attached with the system of springs. Springs are kept in a stretched position with some extension when the system is released. The horizontal surface is assumed to be frictionless. The angular frequency will be _______&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fffad789d-7c67-44a7-8ddd-a2eb504f2fc7-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 338px; height: 82px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4290ae", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295d04"}, {"id": "03fed9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295d05"}, {"id": "c9cd1e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295d06"}, {"id": "e17209", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295d07"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295d08", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479a"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b61"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b20"], "question": {"text": "Two simple harmonic waves having equal amplitudes of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and equal frequency of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> are moving along the same direction. The resultant amplitude is also <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The phase difference between the individual waves is _____ degree."}, "options": [{"id": "ce55ea", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295d09"}, {"id": "33c5ee", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295d0a"}, {"id": "cd815a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295d0b"}, {"id": "a350fc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295d0c"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:30.305Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:30.305Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4f862ee0e063d9295e47"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:13:30.304Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:58:01.795Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAllowed": t